course: dictionary
lesson: 4249
title: Many meanings of graphic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Graphic is a good example. In «The game has good graphics», graphics are the pictures, so here it is a noun for pictures.
explain: «The news warned of graphic images.» Here graphic is an adjective, a describing word. The clue is the warning: the pictures show things very clearly and might upset you. Ask yourself what the sentence tells you, then put your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
explain: Graphic also has a special meaning in design. «Graphic design» is the job of making logos, posters and pages look clear and neat. The phrase tells you the topic is art, not something upsetting.
fact: Graphic can be an adjective (a describing word) or a noun (a naming word).
fact: A graphic is a picture, diagram, chart or design, especially one made on a computer.
fact: Graphics are the pictures and images in a computer game, film or book.
fact: A graphic description shows something in very clear, detailed and sometimes upsetting ways.
fact: A «graphic novel» is a comic-style book, and a «graphics card» is a special part of a computer that draws pictures.
exercise: «The game has good graphics, so the pictures look smooth and real.» What are graphics in this sentence? | The sound and music | The name of the game's maker | The rules for scoring points | *The pictures and images in the game
exercise: «The news warned viewers that the film had graphic violence.» What does graphic mean here? | Funny and silly | *Very clear, realistic and possibly upsetting | Made of paper | Very quiet
exercise: Nadia says a chart is a graphic. Why is that correct? | A chart means the same as a joke | A chart is always a long story | A chart is a type of game | *A chart is a diagram that shows information in a picture
test: «Comics and graphic novels are real reading, because the words and pictures tell the story together.» What is a graphic novel? | *A comic-style book | A school register | A map of the world | A computer game
test: «We learned graphic design in art, making posters look clear and neat.» What does graphic design mean? | Writing long stories | Designing new roads | Playing music | *The art of making things look clear and neat
exam: Which meaning of graphic fits «a graphic description of the crash, with broken glass and blood»? | A computer picture | Cheerful and bright | Drawing and design | *Very clear, detailed and upsetting
